   "section": "Upper Division Laboratory",
   "notes": "Students must complete two upper division laboratory courses.\n- Option 1: Students complete the requirement with a combination of independent study/research and coursework.\n- Option 2: Students complete the requirement with two courses.\nOption 1: independent study or research plus one laboratory course: Students may use Independent Study or Research units towards the upper division lab requirement. This may be fulfilled by one course of independent study/research taken for three or four units. Alternatively, students may combine two semesters of independent study/research taken for two units each. Together the two courses will count as ONE lab requirement. Courses must be completed with a letter grade of C- or higher. If the course is only offered P/NP, then the course must be completed with a P.\nOption 1: independent study or research plus one laboratory course: If a student is using Independent Study/Research for one of the upper division lab requirements, then the student must fulfill the second upper division lab requirement with a laboratory course from the Upper Division Biological Sciences Core (Area A or Area B) or Area of Concentration requirements. Courses must be completed with a letter grade of C- or higher. If the course is only offered P/NP, then the course must be completed with a P.\nOption 2: two laboratory courses: Students must complete two upper division laboratory courses. These courses are selected from the Upper Division Biological Sciences Core (Area A or Area B) or Area of Concentration requirements. Courses must be completed with a letter grade of C- or higher. If the course is only offered P/NP, then the course must be completed with a P.",
